@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Live observation and exact native settlement
+
+`history_observation_poll` shares the immutable history snapshot cut and a bounded, contiguous worker observation
+sequence. Native source records carry mutation/context counters and actual native entry/leaf IDs. Source append,
+rewrite, deletion/reparent (rebuild), leaf and context changes remain observable. A lost/evicted journal cursor fails
+`history_observation_gap`. Direct mutable retained-payload rewrites discovered by coherent capture emit
+`native_untracked_rewrite`. Stop the affected projection and reopen after any incompatible source change or gap.
+
+`message_start`, `message_update`, `message_final`, provisional `message_decision` and final `message_settlement` carry a native lifecycle identity scoped by
+worker, source, native Session, native context and initiating branch leaf. The identity is stamped before asynchronous
+display delivery; filtered or reordered stdout cannot change it. Tool results additionally carry the initiating
+assistant message identity when that exact native context has retained the call. An absent owner requires explicit
+failure/reopen, never pairing a reusable raw tool ID across contexts. Tool-owner associations are bounded to 4096.
+Final readable content supersedes partial reconstructions. Internal custom/configuration/provider state is not exposed.
+
+Settlement happens at AgentSession's actual append/no-append decision. Queued decisions capture the initiating
+lifecycle before yielding, even if the same original object is immediately reused for a newer lifecycle.
+A bounded unresolved empty-error association that is reused before finalization reports explicit failure. An original object append association and
+the existing assistant entry Symbol provide authoritative IDs; no text, timestamp, hash or append adjacency joins
+are used. A native duplicate without an original-object association explicitly reports `no_entry` with
+`native_deduplicated_without_link`; this lifecycle appended no new entry and does not claim an old entry association.
+One-run contexts, classifier refusals, consumed rewind results and replaced prompt generations report explicit
+no-entry reasons. Empty-error skipping is provisional: real terminal recovery may later append the same original
+object. `message_decision` describes that skip; exactly one final `message_settlement` follows recovery append or
+agent-end maintenance. A late original-object frame retains its Symbol identity and cannot create a second row. A throwing native decision reports `failed`. Entries observed in memory report `observed`
+and **durability `not_attested`**. Ordinary append may be lazy or latch write failures; this API never promises durable
+recovery. Recoverable submission/commit receipts require a separate capability.
+
+Snapshot items include retained lifecycle associations so snapshot/live overlap can be excluded by exact identity.
+Those associations are process-local and bounded to 4096; eviction emits `native_settlement_evicted` and invalidates
+an existing derived projection. Old cold entries remain readable, with no invented historical live identity.
+Oversized or unrepresentable live data emits `native_live_gap`; no successful truncated live message is returned.
+Native observation does not cancel or recreate Interactions or execution, and does not alter collaboration callbacks.
+
+## One immutable cut with live handoff
+
+`history_snapshot_open({scope, handoff: "live"})` opts into bounded append/prefix progress while pages continue
+returning the original immutable cut. The default `handoff: "current"` preserves strict #34 invalidation on any
+content change. The `live` cursor belongs to that SAME snapshot and contains unresolved ended runtime messages
+(`livePhase: "ended"`) and the actual current prefix (`livePhase: "streaming"`), with exact native identities.
+`running` retains the complete current readable runtime view. Completed runtime objects also carry their native
+final settlement when known; an absent settlement is never a durable claim.
+
+The opt-in validator verifies exact prior header and retained-entry fingerprints, source, Session and runtime
+context (system prompt, model, thinking and tool schemas), plus bounded contiguous post-cut mutation records.
+Retained runtime messages must stay a stable prefix; a replacement/reorder emits `native_runtime_replaced`.
+An exact pending original object's final settlement may materialize its final accounting. Appended runtime
+messages require their stamped lifecycle identity or native original-object entry association. Only appended
+source records that preserve the active leaf or directly extend its prior parent, and runtime prefix progress,
+may advance. An append that selects an older branch, any context/config change, retained
+rewrite/delete/reparent, source replacement, compaction, observed gap or association eviction rejects the cursor.
+Fingerprints establish revision consistency only; they never associate a message with an entry. Even a newly
+appended entry changed between its append callback and first capture emits `native_untracked_rewrite`.
+
+Native lazy error classification is materialized before assistant entry publication, so later classification
+cannot mutate an already-published entry merely by memoizing `errorId`. The complete field remains fingerprinted.
+Unknown native entry/message/content categories emit an explicit live gap rather than a successful truncated row.
+Poll payloads are capped at 128 events / 768 KiB; per-event cap is 512 KiB and retained live journal is 4096 / 8 MiB.
+
+A consumer buffers post-cut observations by exact native identity while reading immutable pages, then publishes
+one derived baseline. If ordering or association cannot be represented within its bounds it fails the view and
+requires a fresh full-view binding. This option does not reset DSH, replay execution or coordinate viewer holders.
